  "intro": "The Ukrainian alphabet with the sound of every letter, the main reading rules, and a key to the symbols in the pronunciations.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "How the Ukrainian alphabet works",
      "text": [
        "Ukrainian is written in its own version of the Cyrillic alphabet: 33 letters plus the apostrophe. If you know Russian, watch out — the letters overlap but don't all sound the same: Ukrainian г is a voiced h, и is like the i in \"bit\", е is a plain e, and і, ї, є and ґ are Ukrainian-only letters.",
        "Ukrainian is read much as it's written. Unlike Russian, unstressed vowels keep their full sound, and consonants keep their voice at the end of a word (хліб [xlʲib]). The consonants д, т, з, с, ц, л, н are softened before і, є, ю, я and the soft sign ь."
      ]
    },
