    {
      "heading": "Reading rules",
      "text": [
        "Stress: each word has one stressed syllable, and it can fall anywhere; ordinary text doesn't mark it, so the IPA in this app always shows it with ˈ.",
        "в is said as a short w at the end of a syllable (вчора [ˈwtʃɔrɑ], лев [lɛw]), and as a soft v-like [ʋ] before a vowel.",
        "Doubled consonants are long: питання [pɪˈtɑnʲːɑ]."
      ]
    },
